## Why This Is Asked
End-to-end tracing across HTTP, DB, Kafka, and Redis helps diagnose issues that span services and reveals propagation gaps.

## Key Concepts
- OpenTelemetry
- Trace Context propagation
- Span lifetimes and sampling
- Exporters and collectors

## Code Example
```javascript
// Minimal OpenTelemetry setup and propagation
const tracer = opentelemetry.trace.getTracer('cnpa');
app.use((req, res, next) => {
  const span = tracer.startSpan('HTTP '+ req.path);
  req.span = span;
  res.on('finish', ()=> span.end());
  next();
});
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you verify traces in the collector UI?
- How would you handle retry loops that disrupt trace continuity?

## Why This Is Asked
Production CNPA systems require robust observability to diagnose performance issues during peak loads. This tests practical knowledge of distributed systems debugging and real-world monitoring strategies.

## Key Concepts
- Distributed tracing with OpenTelemetry
- Context propagation across service boundaries
- Tail latency analysis and SLA management
- Performance monitoring and alerting thresholds
- Load testing and canary deployment strategies

## Code Example
```javascript
// OpenTelemetry configuration for CNPA pipeline
const { NodeSDK } = require('@opentelemetry/sdk-node');
const { HttpInstrumentation } = require('@opentelemetry/instrumentation-http');
const { PgInstrumentation } = require('@opentelemetry/instrumentation-pg');
const { RedisInstrumentation } = require('@opentelemetry/instrumentation-redis');

const sdk = new NodeSDK({
  instrumentations: [
    new HttpInstrumentation(),
    new PgInstrumentation(),
    new RedisInstrumentation()
  ],
  serviceName: 'cnpa-service'
});

// Kafka context propagation example
const produceWithTracing = async (topic, message, span) => {
  const headers = {
    traceparent: span.spanContext().traceparent,
    'x-request-id': span.spanContext().traceId
  };
  await producer.send({ topic, messages: [{ value: message, headers }] });
};
```

## Why This Is Asked
In CNPA stacks, authentication rotation can create bottlenecks that affect all requests; this question evaluates your ability to diagnose cross-service latency and implement effective auth caching strategies.

## Key Concepts
- Distributed tracing across HTTP, database, Kafka, and Redis services
- JWKS caching and cache staleness trade-offs
- Resource pooling and batch processing optimization
- Canary validation and metrics-driven verification

## Code Example
```javascript
// JWKS cache example
const jwksCache = new Map();
async function getKeys(kid){
  const cached = jwksCache.get(kid);
  if (cached && !isExpired(cached)) {
    return cached.keys;
  }
  const keys = await fetchJWKS();
  jwksCache.set(kid, { keys, timestamp: Date.now() });
  return keys;
}
```

## Why This Is Asked

Tests the ability to design practical backpressure and degradation strategies for a CNPA stack under load, balancing user impact with data integrity.

## Key Concepts

- Backpressure and load shedding
- Degraded paths and asynchronous processing
- Idempotency and deduplication across HTTP, DB, and Kafka
- Observability: latency, error rate, queue depth, saturation signals

## Code Example

```javascript
class TokenBucket {
  constructor(rate, burst) {
    this.rate = rate; // tokens per second
    this.burst = burst; // max tokens
    this.tokens = burst;
    this.last = Date.now();
  }
  consume(n = 1) {
    this._refresh();
    if (this.tokens >= n) {
      this.tokens -= n;
      return true;
    }
    return false;
  }
  _refresh() {
    const now = Date.now();
    const elapsed = (now - this.last) / 1000;
    this.tokens = Math.min(this.burst, this.tokens + elapsed * this.rate);
    this.last = now;
  }
}
```

